Rāvaṇa marches himself after Prahasta falls --- Vibhīṣaṇa names Akampana Indrajit Atikāya and chiefs for Rāma --- Rāvaṇa shatters Sugrīva hurled peak and fells Sugrīva --- Rāvaṇa wounds Gavākṣa and chiefs and routs monkey host --- Lakṣmaṇa gains leave while Hanumān staggers Rāvaṇa with palm --- Rāvaṇa fells Hanumān with fist then batters Nīla --- Nīla dances on banner bow and crown before Āgnēya arrow fells him --- Lakṣmaṇa withstands forehead arrow and severs Rāvaṇa bow --- Rāvaṇa pierces Lakṣmaṇa with Brahmā Śakti but cannot lift him --- Hanumān bears Lakṣmaṇa to Rāma as Rāma wrecks chariot cuts crown and spares Rāvaṇa